# box-mounts — what the agent boxes can see, decided per project (edit from the hub with
# `cbx expose` / `cbx hide`, or by hand). All sources are confined under the checkout by the
# broker. Recreate a box (cbx kill + cbx box) to apply changes.
#
# Grammar (whitespace-separated; '#'/blank ignored):
#   TREE <dst> <ro|rw>     mount the WHOLE checkout at /home/dev/<dst>, with <dst>/.git shadowed
#                          (agents edit everything but never see .git); also sets the box workdir
#   <src> <dst> <ro|rw>    mount checkout/<src> at /home/dev/<dst>
#
# Default: whole working tree, writable, .git hidden — only the hub can git/commit/push.
TREE checkout rw

# Examples of finer control instead of TREE:

# Full repo, but .git read-only
#  .      checkout       rw
#  .git   checkout/.git  ro

# Full repo, but .git writable (agent still unable to push, as it's missing repo credentials)
#  .      checkout       rw
#  .git   checkout/.git  ro

# Only parts of the repo, partly read-only
#   src           src            rw
#   package.json  package.json   ro
#   checkout/.git checkout/.git  ro     # expose history read-only if agents need `git diff/log`
